{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.LambdaScaleAbsorbed","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.LambdaScaleAbsorbed","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.no_separate_lambda_scale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.no_separate_lambda_scale","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/LambdaScaleAbsorbed.lean#L72-L82","doc":"**No separate λ_scale.** The antipattern class is provably\nimpossible: it is uninhabited (`IsEmpty`).  This is a genuine\nderivation — given any putative instance we reach `False` through\nits `is_antipattern` field — *stated* as the non-degenerate\n`IsEmpty SeparateLambdaScale_Antipattern`, not a bare projection\nof `False`.  Use it (`#check no_separate_lambda_scale`) as the\ntype-level record that no separate `λ_scale` object exists; the\nmass formula is `m(K) = m_e × VolDensity(K, q₀)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.SeparateLambdaScale_Antipattern.is_antipattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.SeparateLambdaScale_Antipattern.is_antipattern","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/LambdaScaleAbsorbed.lean#L70-L70","doc":"This field is `False` — class is unsatisfiable. The antipattern\nis \"treating λ_scale as a separate object\" (purged 2026-05-24). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.SeparateLambdaScale_Antipattern.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.SeparateLambdaScale_Antipattern.mk","kind":"ctor","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/LambdaScaleAbsorbed.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.SeparateLambdaScale_Antipattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.SeparateLambdaScale_Antipattern","kind":"class","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/LambdaScaleAbsorbed.lean#L62-L70","doc":"**The absorption is observable** at the type level: any Lean\nfunction that takes a separate `λ_scale : ℝ` argument is doing the\nwrong thing. This conditional class is intentionally **unsatisfiable**\n(no instance can be provided) to flag the antipattern at the\ntype-class resolution layer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.lambdaScaleAbsorbedIntoGeom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.lambdaScaleAbsorbedIntoGeom","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/LambdaScaleAbsorbed.lean#L49-L60","doc":"**Inert marker** recording the 2026-05-23 absorption of\n`λ_scale` into the canonical per-knot `VolDensity(K)` evaluation.\n\nThis is intentionally a `Unit`-valued constant: there is **no**\nsubstantive λ_scale to define. The mass formula is\n`m(K) = m_e × VolDensity(K, q₀)` — single Geom call, no separate\nλ_scale constant.\n\nUse this constant as a documentation anchor (`#check\nlambdaScaleAbsorbedIntoGeom`) when downstream code seems to assume\na separate `λ_scale`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}